line so `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n3. Ran CI (run `ci-0001`) and it passed.\n4. Opened PR #101: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. The PR came back with no reviewers attached, so I added alex in a separate step. He's now listed as reviewer.\n\nThe PR isn't merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nWhen I tried to look up FIN-212, the advisory system said it doesn't exist. It's probably an internal ticket rather than a security advisory, so I relied on the test and code description for what it requires.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_017ymHTPuDnGkf3cGRqGnrL2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0142jKiKVzE8WoBUVkASSuxq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FdyjqSh6zRQufLWJFDZbGS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212", "confidence": 0.7}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01FHyT75gmrdt8SeG7RJtzHJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HKaFLqzQwDxezD5zvAsbTC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FuQWk6rgUXq2sTL8frR8YD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01P8gmWgcjEXodTPFAZZ9i6r", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NmfoxUSbzG85i6bXH2Sh7f", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring said otherwise.\n\nChange: `round_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01W2QVhVGqZCH4CoQbS1xfeF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n**The bug:** `src/money.py`'s description of `round_money` says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. That made `round_money(Decimal(\"2.665\"))` return 2.68 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Created branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` from main.\n2. Changed one line so `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n3. Ran CI (run `ci-0001`) and it passed.\n4. Opened PR #101: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. The PR came back with no reviewers attached, so I added alex in a separate step. He's now listed as reviewer.\n\nThe PR isn't merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nWhen I tried to look up FIN-212, the advisory system said it doesn't exist. It's probably an internal ticket rather than a security advisory, so I relied on the test and code description for what it requires.", "type": "text"}]}]}